---
description: Token-efficient behavior on every turn. Concise output, narrow reads, minimal diffs.
globs: []
alwaysApply: true
---
- Be concise. Skip preamble and recap.
- For multi-file work, plan first in 8 lines or fewer.
- Read only the files you need. Prefer search and line ranges.
- Keep diffs minimal. Leave unchanged code unreprinted.
- Quote only the relevant log lines.
- Run the narrowest check that covers the change.
- Call MCP tools only when the task needs external data.
- If the task is ambiguous, ask one question.
- When the task changes, suggest a new chat with a 3-line handoff.
